Chapter 4: Intelligence Gathering helped me connect the dots on mistakes I have made that caused me to struggle with research and information gathering in the past. My first mistake was going into research with the wrong goal. I was starting out by just searching for a source that would answer my question or contain the information I needed, rather than trying to gain a broad understanding of what is already known about the topic, what the arguments are, and where the gaps are. The conversation metaphor made it click for me why the literature review step is so important, and this perspective will guide how I do research moving forward. My second problem was organizing my search. In the past I chose one or two databases, searched for a while, and simply kept the articles I found relevant open in dozens of browser tabs to sort through later, which led to me forgetting what each one was about. Combining a research organization software with the textbook's three step research method will help me overcome this problem and do much better, more thorough and organized research.
